<title>MEXICO: Mexico's March coffee exports rise from March '96.</title>
<headline>Mexico's March coffee exports rise from March '96.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican coffee exports totalled 651,495 60-kg bags in March, compared to the 631,513 bags sent abroad in the same month in 1996, the Mexican Coffee Council said in a report obtained by Reuters on Friday.</p>
<p>The council, the government umbrella organization covering the nation's coffee sector, said the export figure represented a 3.2 percent rise from March 1996.  </p>
<p>The coffee figures for March are preliminary, and the report revised some past export numbers.</p>
<p>The council said Mexico's exports for the first six months of the 1996-1997 cycle totalled 3,235,070 bags of coffee, compared to the 2,939,623 bags in the same period for the 1995-1996 crop.</p>
<p>A full breakdown of the Mexican exports follows in table form. Figures are for 60-kg bags.</p>
<p>    Month	 1996-1997	 1995-1996	    1994-1995</p>
<p>    October	163,489	   101,912		 59,303</p>
<p>    November     320,842	   296,810		131,767</p>
<p>    December     390,111	   421,445		260,081</p>
<p>    January	875,904	   745,428		586,669</p>
<p>    February     837,812	   742,815		460,060</p>
<p>    March	  651,495	   631,513		603,537</p>
<p>    April				528,944		243,772</p>
<p>    May				  456,768		287,238</p>
<p>    June				 193,627		217,951</p>
<p>    July				 219,432		121,033</p>
<p>    August			     146,745		184,466</p>
<p>    September			   86,982		101,867</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
